  "term": "EPQ",
  "definition": "EPQ usually refers to the Eysenck Personality Questionnaire, a personality measure that includes neuroticism as one of its main dimensions. In this context, neuroticism refers to a stable tendency toward emotional instability, stronger reactions to negative events, and difficulty controlling impulses and emotions.",
